# Somebody new on the mesh, seen from wherever the reader happens to be.
#
# The Nodes tab's badge counts the nodes discovered since the reader last stood on the tab, and
# going there is what clears it - the rule a tab badge is held to. On the tab, the new rows say
# "new" first on their quiet line and stand out in strong ink until the reader leaves and comes
# back. The notice is the app's; there is no app behind the harness, so it is raised here in the
# words the app would use.

scene demo
tab messages
hold 900

discover RDGE Ridge Relay
toast New node: RDGE
hold 1800

discover HUT2 Upper Hut
discover LKOT Lookout Tower
toast 2 new nodes
hold 1800

# Going there clears the badge, and the three rows say which they are.
tab nodes
hold 2200

# Away and back: they have been seen.
tab messages
hold 700
tab nodes
hold 1600
